issue_body:
The PipelineProcessor unzips the pipeline output if it detects it is a zip, however, CBZ is a zip archive--so CBZ pipelines unintentionally unzip the contents (images) into the output folder.

Expected behaviour:
A `*.cbz` file to be placed in the `finishedFolders`.

Relevant function:
https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-PDF/blob/620ed930d9810a093ea52c5620f19537b7e7f6c9/app/core/src/main/java/stirling/software/SPDF/controller/api/pipeline/PipelineProcessor.java#L382C1-L388C6

I am using Pipeline with watched folders.

For reference, this is my pipeline JSON:
```json
{
  "name": "pdf-to-cbz",
  "pipeline": [
    {
      "operation": "/api/v1/convert/pdf/cbz",
      "parameters": {
        "dpi": 300,
        "fileInput": "automated"
      }
    }
  ],
  "outputDir": "{outputFolder}/pdf-to-cbz",
  "outputFileName": "{filename}"
}
```

